{title: We Shall See The King}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]There's a blessed time that's [A7]coming, coming [D]soon
It may be evening, morning, or at [A7]noon
The [D]wedding of the [D7]bride, u[G]nited with the [D]groom
We shall see the [A7]King when He [D]comes

{comment: Chorus}
[D]We shall see the King, We shall see the King,
We shall see the [E7]King when He [A7]comes,
[D]He is coming in [D7]power, we'll [G]hail the blessed [D]hour,
[D]We shall see the [A7]king when He [D]comes

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Are you ready should the [A7]savior call [D]today?
Would Jesus say "Well done or go [A7]away"?
"[D]My home is for the [D7]pure, the [G]vile can never [D]stay"
We shall see the [A7]King when He [D]comes

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Oh, my brother are rea[A7]dy for the [D]call?
To crown your savior King and Lord of [A7]all?
[D]The kingdoms of this [D7]world shall [G]soon before Him [D]fall
We shall see the [A7]King when He [D]comes
